{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "id": "complaint-deadlines",
  "title": "Complaint handling deadlines",
  "turns": [
    {
      "jobId": "2c207b13-a0bc-48d5-8e1f-0901d1787788",
      "question": "A customer complains that their loan modification request was denied. How soon must the bank acknowledge and resolve the complaint, and when does it escalate to the Complaint Resolution Team?",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-04T05:32:18.743631Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-04T05:32:22.765568Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "Based on the Harborview Community Bank's **Customer Complaint Handling Procedure (v4.0, effective 1 May 2026)**, a complaint about a denied loan modification falls under the **\"Lending and loan servicing\"** category (which explicitly includes \"modification denials\" as an example) [1].\n\n| Action | Timeline | Notes |\n|--------|----------|-------|\n| **Acknowledge** | Within **2 business days** of logging the complaint | Written acknowledgement with reference number, handler name, and expected response date |\n| **Resolve** | Within **15 business days** of logging the complaint | Owner: Loan Servicing |\n| **Escalation to Complaint Resolution Team** | **Automatically on the 10th business day** if not yet resolved | Team may extend resolution by up to 15 additional business days (with written notice to customer before the original deadline) |\n\nBusiness days exclude weekends and bank holidays, counted from the day after the complaint is logged. A complaint open more than 30 business days is reported to the Head of Customer Care weekly and to the Compliance Committee at its next meeting.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Unstructured Retrieval evidence — complaint_handling_procedure.docx — evidence `hermes-receipt:7b7bc1ed0fa3f25f15ac2a2e6e3091db176421fe2848983cbfccd4d5a0ff786c`",
        "citations": [
          {
            "number": 1,
            "evidenceId": "hermes-receipt:7b7bc1ed0fa3f25f15ac2a2e6e3091db176421fe2848983cbfccd4d5a0ff786c",
