                "publishedAt": null,
                "snippet": "Customer Complaint Handling Procedure\n6. Escalation\nIf a complaint has not been resolved by the 10th business day, it is escalated automatically to the Complaint Resolution Team, a group of senior specialists who are independent of the owner. The Team may extend the resolution time by up to 15 business days when the investigation needs information from a third party, such as a card network or merchant. The customer must be told in writing before the original deadline expires, with the reason and the new date. A complaint that is open more than 30 business days is reported to the Head of Customer Care weekly and to the Compliance Committee at its next meeting.\nA customer who is not satisfied with the final response may ask for a review by the Chief Compliance Officer, whose decision is final within the Bank. The response letter must tell customers that they may also contact the Bank's primary federal regulator or the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau at any time.",
                "metadata": {
                  "parser": "docling-docx",
                  "file_id": "f-cf35b7218f0c2c45",
