                "title": "complaint_handling_procedure.docx",
                "url": null,
                "publishedAt": null,
                "snippet": "Customer Complaint Handling Procedure\n5. Investigation steps\n1. **Acknowledge.** Send a written acknowledgement within the time in Table 1 that gives the reference number, the name of the person handling the complaint and the date by which the customer will receive an answer.\n2. **Investigate.** The owner reviews the account history, call recordings and relevant policies, and speaks with every employee involved. The investigator may not be the person who is the subject of the complaint.\n3. **Decide and respond.** The owner decides, in plain language, whether the complaint is upheld, partly upheld or not upheld, explains why, and states any remedy, such as a fee refund or a correction to credit reporting.\n4. **Close.** The owner records the outcome, the remedy and the root cause in the complaint system and closes the case only after the response has been sent.",
                "metadata": {
                  "parser": "docling-docx",
