                "title": "complaint_handling_procedure.docx",
                "url": null,
                "publishedAt": null,
                "snippet": "Customer Complaint Handling Procedure\n2. What counts as a complaint\nA complaint is any expression of dissatisfaction, written or spoken, about the Bank's products, services or employees, whether or not the customer uses the word \"complaint\". A simple question or a request for information is an inquiry and is answered on the spot. If an inquiry cannot be answered at once, or the customer is unhappy with the answer, it becomes a complaint.",
